id: bluetooth_agents_controller
label: Bluetooth controller agents.md contributions
package: bluetooth_le_controller
description: >
  Bluetooth Controller usage contributions for agents.md
quality: evaluation
provides:
- name: bluetooth_agents_controller
template_contribution:
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_hci
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_hci
    context: |
      # Bluetooth HCI for Silicon Labs Series2 and Series3 Devices
      This provides HCI interface with the bluetooth controller. HCI is the interface between
      Bluetooth Host and Bluetooth Controller.
      ## Supported Commands and Features
      Supported commands and features can be read by issuing HCI_Read_Local_Supported_Commands
      and HCI_LE_Read_Local_Supported_Features_Page_0 commands. Based on the components required
      by the project, the respective features, commands and events will be supported.
      ## HCI transport
      There are multiple streams for HCI transport, UART is the default transport, but CPC
      and 3-wire could also be selected.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_advertiser
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_advertiser
    context: |
      # Bluetooth Advertising For Silicon Labs Series2 and Series3 Devices
      This provides Bluetooth Advertising feature.
      Before starting advertising the user must set advertising parameters and data.
      Based on the used advertising type, the user might need to set advertising data, and / or scan response data.
      ## Constraints
      The maximum advertising interval supported is 0xFFFF / 40959.375 ms, if the user tries with
      a larger interval the parameters will be rejected.
      ## Legacy Advertising
      In Legacy advertisements, data length is limited to 31 bytes. Usually for more than 31
      bytes it is good to use scannable advertisements, then in the scan response the user
      could add 31 bytes of data.
      Legacy advertisements can be connectable scannable, which is the most common for peripheral
      use case, or directed connectable, scannable, non-connectable / non-scannable.
      ### Constraints
      If the user attempts to advertise more than 31 bytes the data will be rejected.
      Legacy advertisements use primary advertising channels which have bigger traffic so there is
      high chance of conflicts and CRC errors.
      ## Extended Advertising
      Extended advertisements can be only one of connectable, scannable, or non-connectable / non
      scannable.
      ### Constraints
      In extended advertising, data length could be up to 1650 bytes. Data must fit within one
      interval otherwise advertisements will be rejected.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_scanner
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_scanner
    context: |
      # Bluetooth Scanning For Silicon Labs Series2 and Series3 Devices
      This provides Bluetooth Scanning feature.
      Before starting the scanning, the user must set scanning parameters.
      Scanning window and interval are used to calculate scanning duty cycle as follows
      duty cycle = window / interval, max duty cycle is 100%.
      ## Constraints
      Based on how fast the application is consuming the advertising reports sent by the
      controller, it is possible that the controller would run out of buffer and it would throttle
      the system, especially when scanning at 100% duty cycle for longer periods. It is
      recommended to consume the advertising reports as soon as possible, or use filtering.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_connection_role_central
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_connection_role_central
    context: |
      # Bluetooth Connection Central For Silicon Labs Series2 and Series3 Devices
      This provides Bluetooth Central Connection feature.
      In order to setup central connection, the application must start scanning to find the
      advertising devices that are using connectable advertising. Then create a connection
      to a device based on the advertiser's Bluetooth address.
      ## Constraints
      By default phy update feature is not included to save flash and memory, to use it include
      `bluetooth_feature_connection_phy_update` component.
      The max number of connections supported is 32 connections, or less based on the memory
      availability in the device. When using multiple connections it is good to have system
      understanding and design, if the goal is to have the least latency, then it is recommended
      to use `bluetooth_controller_anchor_selection` component.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_connection_role_peripheral
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_connection_role_peripheral
    context: |
      # Bluetooth Connection Peripheral For Silicon Labs Series2 and Series3 Devices
      This provides Bluetooth Peripheral Connection feature.
      In order to setup peripheral connection, the application must start connectable advertising,
      then a central device would establish a connection with the peripheral device. If the
      application starts scannable only advertising, then a connection can never be established.
      Once connection is established the advertising set that was started is stopped by the
      controller.
      ## Constraints
      By default phy update feature is not included to save flash and memory, to use it include
      `bluetooth_feature_connection_phy_update` component.
      The max number of connections supported is 32 connections, or less based on the memory
      availability in the device. However, in peripheral connection the Bluetooth controller
      cannot schedule the connections based on its own timings because that is decided by
      the central device(s). This means that peripheral connections cannot scale with all
      interval and timeout parameters without a good system design and understanding.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_cs
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_cs
    context: |
      # Bluetooth Channel Sounding For Silicon Labs Series2 and Series3 Devices
      This provides Bluetooth Channel Sounding (CS) feature for high-accuracy
      distance measurement using phase-based ranging and round-trip time (RTT).
      Channel Sounding requires a connection between two devices. Before
      starting CS procedures, the application must exchange CS capabilities with
      the remote device, enable CS security, create a CS configuration, and set
      procedure parameters.
      ## Constraints
      Channel Sounding is only supported on devices with CS-capable hardware.
      The link layers of the connected devices negotiate and decide the subevent length, the
      application cannot preset a subevent length.
      CS SYNC PHY is the PHY used for CS packets (mode0, mode1, RTT portion of mode3), that is
      different from connection PHY. CS SYNC PHYs and device supported PHYs do not necessarily match.
      CS requires larger Bluetooth buffer, and higher UART baudrate to deliver CS subevents
      results as fast as possible, otherwise aborts of multiple subevents happen more frequently.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_sync
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_sync
    context: |
      # Bluetooth Periodic Advertising Synchronization For Silicon Labs Series2 and Series3 Devices
      This provides Bluetooth Periodic Advertising Synchronization feature.
      Periodic advertising synchronization allows a device to synchronize to periodic
      advertising trains from another device, receiving data at regular intervals without
      a connection. Before creating a sync, the application must be scanning to discover
      periodic advertisers. Synchronization can also be established via PAST (Periodic
      Advertising Sync Transfer) over an existing connection if `bluetooth_feature_sync_past`
      is included. Once synchronized, the controller delivers periodic advertising reports
      to the host. If the sync is lost (e.g., due to timeout), the application must
      re-create the sync.
      ## Constraints
      The max number of simultaneous syncs depends on memory
      availability in the device. Maintaining multiple simultaneous syncs is further
      constrained by the fact that periodic advertisers operate independently and know
      nothing about each other, which can cause scheduling conflicts and missed events
      when their timing overlaps.

ui_hints:
  visibility: never

metadata:
  sbom:
    license: MSLA
root_path: bluetooth_le_controller
